# SVG assets

Illustrations and reusable icons live as `.svg` files under `src/assets/`, not as large inline `<svg>` trees in Vue SFCs.

## Layout

```
src/assets/
  icons/          # close, email, password, …
  auth/           # auth scene art
  landing/        # landing illustrations (when added)
```

Kebab-case file names. Group by feature or `icons/` for shared UI glyphs.

## How to use

1. Put the graphic in `src/assets/.../*.svg`.
2. Import it with Vite `?raw` and inject once (static trusted asset only):

```vue
<template>
  <span class="app-input__icon" aria-hidden="true" v-html="iconEmail" />
</template>
<script setup lang="ts">
import iconEmail from '@/assets/icons/email.svg?raw'
</script>
```

3. Color via `currentColor` / CSS classes on the SVG, and theme tokens in CSS (`var(--color-*)`) — no hex in Vue or SVG fills when the seasonal theme should control the look.

## Allowed exceptions

- Tiny, **data-bound** SVG (e.g. progress ring whose `stroke-dashoffset` is computed in the component).
- One-off path that cannot be reused and is under ~5 short elements — prefer assets anyway if it will be reused.

## Do not

```vue
<!-- BAD — illustration pasted into the SFC -->
<template>
  <svg viewBox="0 0 1440 900">…dozens of paths…</svg>
</template>
```

```vue
<!-- GOOD -->
<template>
  <div class="auth-scene__art" v-html="forestScene" />
</template>
<script setup lang="ts">
import forestScene from '@/assets/auth/forest-scene.svg?raw'
</script>
```

Do not add SVG loader libraries unless asked. Do not `v-html` user-provided SVG.
